Sval: a tab's scoped permissions outlive its subframes

PermissionManager::Observe clears every permission scoped to a tab
(RemoveAllForBrowser) on "browsing-context-discarded" for any browsing
context carrying the tab's BrowserId. A subframe carries its tab's
BrowserId, and every load of a page that has frames discards them, so a
reload or a removed iframe took away a grant SitePermissions' "allow
now" or Sval's media button had just given, while the tab stayed. Only a
top-level context's discard ends the tab; a replaced one is skipped
already.

diff --git a/extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.cpp b/extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.cpp
index 91024de98..4690fa3e9 100644
--- a/extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.cpp
+++ b/extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.cpp
@@ -3120,7 +3120,11 @@ NS_IMETHODIMP PermissionManager::Observe(nsISupports* aSubject,
       nsCOMPtr<nsILoadContext> loadContext = do_QueryInterface(aSubject);
       if (loadContext) {
         auto* bc = static_cast<BrowsingContext*>(loadContext.get());
-        discardedBrowserId = bc->BrowserId();
+        // A subframe shares its tab's BrowserId, and goes away with every
+        // load of its parent page while the tab stays.
+        if (bc->IsTop()) {
+          discardedBrowserId = bc->BrowserId();
+        }
       }
     }
   }
